# The RT kernel is NOT listed here. It comes from --linux-flavours rt-amd64 in
# auto/config, which is what makes it the bootstrap flavour and therefore the
# kernel the default boot entry actually loads. Listing it here as well would
# pull in the generic kernel alongside it.

# Audio server. ADR-0003: PipeWire only, no jackd. pipewire-jack provides the
# API our engine links against.
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
pipewire-jack
libspa-0.2-modules
wireplumber

# Audio tooling the engine and diagnostics need.
alsa-utils

# libjack-jackd2-0 is deliberately NOT here. It installs a libjack.so.0 into
# the default library path, which wins over the one pipewire-jack ships in
# pipewire-0.3/jack/, and our engine then tries to reach a jackd that does not
# exist: "Cannot connect to server socket". The hook makes pipewire-jack the
# system-wide JACK instead.

# Firmware, so unknown hardware has a chance of working on first boot. Listed
# by name: auto/config turns live-build's firmware auto-inclusion off, because
# it installed every archive package with a file under lib/firmware, and the
# b43 installers among them download the Broadcom blob from github.com during
# the build (a 504 there failed the nightly of 2026-11-08). No metapackage
# either: firmware-linux's dependency set is Debian's choice, not this list's.
firmware-linux-free
firmware-misc-nonfree
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-mediatek
firmware-libertas
firmware-ti-connectivity
firmware-bnx2
firmware-bnx2x
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-intel-misc
firmware-intel-sound
firmware-sof-signed

# Storage for session disks.
e2fsprogs
exfatprogs
dosfstools
parted

# Minimum to run the engine on a tty with no desktop.
kbd
console-setup
util-linux

# Diagnostics. An appliance that cannot be debugged in the room is not useful.
pciutils
usbutils
htop
less
nano

# Display stack (ADR-0010). Inert unless the kernel command line has
# sonora.gui. libpam-systemd is listed explicitly: without it libseat1 is
# satisfied by the seatd daemon instead of logind.
libpam-systemd
labwc
xwayland
# Qt runtime for sonora-ui, from what it links and imports rather than from
# its build image: find_package(Qt6 ... Core Gui Qml Quick) in ui/qt, and the
# QML imports only QtQuick and the module it registers itself. The rest of
# what ldd shows (QtQml, QtOpenGL, QtNetwork, QtDBus, the QtQml and
# WorkerScript QML modules) comes in as dependencies of these three. No
# Controls, Templates or Widgets: nothing in ui/qt uses them.
qt6-wayland
libqt6quick6
qml6-module-qtquick
qml6-module-qtquick-window
libgl1-mesa-dri
libglx-mesa0
libegl-mesa0
fonts-dejavu-core

# sonora-install (ADR-0032): partitioning, copying the squashfs the stick
# booted, and the boot loader for both firmware paths. fdisk provides sfdisk.
fdisk
squashfs-tools
efibootmgr
grub-efi-amd64-bin
grub-pc-bin
grub-common

# sonora-plugin-host (ADR-0007 section 3): lilv loads LV2 bundles, libx11 opens
# out-of-process editors on labwc's Xwayland. Named from what the binary links,
# not from its build image's -dev packages. The native bundles in
# /usr/local/lib/{lv2,vst3} need nothing beyond libc.
liblilv-0-0
libx11-6
